gates:
G1 Tue 2026-10-13 (engine), on a real Windows 10/11 x64 PC and on Linux x64. Standalone Java 8 probe with our CCBlueX build:
(a) CEF starts 5 out of 5 times;
(b) at least 25 paints/s at 1280x720 on a 30 fps page;
(c) the relay's VP9+Opus over WebRTC and over LL-HLS plays with audio;
(d) codec build only: an H.264/AAC MP4 and a YouTube embed of a live stream play;
(e) the process tree is gone 5 s after exit.
Outcomes: (a)-(c) and (e) fail on the OBS-150 build but pass on Spotify-152 -> ship 152, relay only. Both fail -> CinemaMod 116 emergency engine, decided by 10-14. (d) fails -> the embed backup is dropped and SN1 becomes the only backup.

G2 Wed 2026-10-14 (relay over WAN, from 2 residential ISPs). Pass needs all of the following:
- added-delay median under 1.0 s for WebRTC and under 3.0 s for LL-HLS;
- 30 minutes with zero stalls longer than 1 s;
- 50 virtual viewers sustained, with relay CPU under 70% and egress matching about 1.9 Mbit/s per viewer.
On failure: switch to the 480p tier or a CDN/LL-HLS-only delivery; if still failing, the embed backup becomes primary (requires the G1 codec build).

G3 Fri 2026-10-16 (in-game), GTNH frozen version on Windows, Java 8 and Java 21/lwjgl3ify, Angelica default. Pass needs:
- relay video and audio on a 16x9 screen;
- no culling when the origin block is off-screen;
- median FPS drop of 25% or less versus the same scene without the telão, on a mid-range PC;
- 10 cycles of join/leave/break/dimension-hop with zero crashes and no lingering audio;
- a dedicated server that boots and loads the screen without natives;
- a missing-natives client joins and sees the placeholder.
On failure: cut the scope (drop keyboard input and the Linux tier) and slip G4 by at most 1 day.

G4 Sun 2026-10-18 20:00 BRT (public rehearsal #1, 10+ players). Pass needs:
- at least 90% of players who passed preflight see video within 15 s of entering range;
- skew between players of 150 ms or less on WebRTC and 250 ms or less on steered LL-HLS, measured by a burned-in clock/frame counter photographed or logged per client;
- zero client crashes attributable to the mod;
- no admin-lock bypass;
- relay egress within plan.
On failure: fix list; LL-HLS-only mode if WebRTC is unreliable over NAT.

G5 Thu 2026-10-22 (rehearsal #2 on RC1). Pass needs:
- all G4 criteria;
- every fallback switch (webrtc -> hls -> embed -> tse -> poster) completes in under 10 s for all clients;
- preflight OK reported by at least 80% of expected attendees (from the telemetry handshake);
- the rights decision documented.

G6 Sat 2026-10-24 22:00 BRT (final go/no-go after the 17:00-20:00 dress rehearsal with the owner's unlisted restream). GO needs:
- G5 criteria still met;
- ingest failover (OBS restart) recovered in under 60 s;
- the owner's restream shows no Content ID interruption with the telão audio muted or the TSE page shown.
NO-GO -> run the event on SN1 (TSE results page in the same in-game browser), clearly labelled as a safety net, with relay video only for staff.

test_matrix:
P0 (must be green by RC1 on 10-20), assuming the frozen version is 2.8.4:
- Win11 + Java 8 + Angelica default;
- Win11 + Java 21 + Angelica default;
- Win10 + Java 8 + Angelica default (low-end iGPU, 8 GB RAM);
- dedicated server with Java 8 and with Java 21 (no natives loaded).
Each cell runs: preflight, relay WebRTC, relay LL-HLS, embed (codec build), TSE page, fallback switch, join/leave/break/dimension hop, exit leaves no helper process, missing natives shows the placeholder.

P1 (by 10-21):
- Win11 + Java 21 + shaders on;
- Linux x64 + Java 8;
- Linux x64 + Java 21;
- Win11 + Java 8 + Angelica off (if the pack allows it);
- Unicode username path 'C:\Users\João Conceição';
- Prism instance name with spaces and parentheses;
- ABNT2 keyboard: admin types 'ação ç $%&' on Java 8 and on Java 21;
- two MC instances at once (profile lock placeholder).

P2 (smoke only, by 10-22, only if the server or players use these versions):
- GTNH 2.9 RC + Java 21 (SDL3 input, Angelica core profile);
- GTNH 2.9 RC + Java 8 (Angelica 2.x core profile on LWJGL2);
- GTNH 2.7.4 + Java 8;
- GTNH 2.7.4 + Java 21.
If the server freezes 2.9, it moves to P0 and 2.8.4 becomes P2.

Placeholder-only cells:
- macOS (Intel and ARM) on Java 8 and Java 21: must join without a crash, show the 'Telão indisponível no macOS' texture, and get SN2 audio if enabled;
- Windows on arm64;
- Win7/8.1.

Load and network tests:
- 50 virtual viewers on the relay (G2);
- a strict-NAT client gets the TCP or LL-HLS fallback;
- 20+ real players at spawn for FPS and egress (G4/G5).

Security tests:
- a non-admin SetURL, Click or Type packet is rejected and audited;
- an internal-IP or file:// URL is rejected server-side and blocked client-side;
- a page navigation or popup to an off-allowlist host is cancelled and reloaded;
- the rate limit triggers on spam.
